<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan gold prices seen soft amid low demand.</title>
<headline>Pakistan gold prices seen soft amid low demand.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan gold prices are likely to remain soft amid low demand for jewellery in local markets and dwindling international gold prices, dealers at the Karachi bullion market said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;Gold demand is very low,&quot; dealer Farooq Qureshi said. &quot;People don't have enough to eat. How will they buy gold?&quot;</p>
<p>Silver prices remained stable, he said.</p>
<p>Weekly prices:</p>
<p>							 Saturday   June 21</p>
<p>    Gold 24 carat in rupees per 10 grams   4,560	4,565</p>
<p>    Silver per 1,000 grammes		   6,600	6,600</p>
<p>($1 = 40.56 rupees) -- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
